    "narrative": "For the June 2nd slate, our primary objective remains securing stolen bases without sacrificing lineup efficiency. **Corbin Carroll** (77.40) stands as our premier play today, leveraging a favorable matchup against Lauer. While the dynamic platoon adjustment against a lefty provides a minor anchor, **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s elite speed profile and second-spot placement create a massive ceiling for runs and steals. Similarly, **Jose Caballero** (70.71) is a mandatory start; despite the #8 hole, his high-tier matchup against Cantillo and a 13% boost from the platoon advantage make him one of our most efficient sources of category production. **Tyler Soderstrom** (65.10) and **Gabriel Moreno** (64.94) round out our top-tier tier, with both benefitting from advantageous SP_xERA matchups that prioritize high-contact outcomes.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today was **Austin Riley** (48.60). Although he possesses the raw talent to outperform his projection, his matchup against Gausman\u2014a strikeout-heavy arm\u2014and unfavorable park wind factors dropped him below our threshold. **Austin Riley** was the closest to cracking the lineup, but the optimizer favored the platoon-advantaged **Jose Caballero** and the favorable lineup position of **Seiya Suzuki** (54.43). We must also exercise caution with our \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Josh Naylor** and **Kyle Karros**; should their confirmed batting orders slip, their daily efficiency scores will adjust downward significantly. Keep a close eye on weather reports, as the \"Wind In\" warnings affecting **Seiya Suzuki** and **Tyler Soderstrom** introduce non-trivial downside risk to their power profiles today.",
